extraction_notes: |
  - Triax and the NGR, printed 197-199, under the heading *Optional Player
    Characters*. SPLIT FROM THE GARGOYLE, which shares its entry: printed 198
    heads the two together and then states them separately at every point that
    matters - two attribute lines, two M.D.C. formulas, two horror factors, two
    running speeds, two leap distances, and a skills list that diverges by
    species. Escape artist is gurgoyle-only and swim is +10% here against the
    gargoyle''s MINUS 10%. The survey called this split before the import.
  - THE GURGOYLE HAS NO WINGS, so the gargoyle''s flight, its 100 foot gliding
    leap, its +4 to dodge in flight and its flying tackle are all absent here.
    Its Spd of 6D6+10 is a plain running speed with no second figure behind it,
    which is the one place this row is simpler than its sibling.
  - THE BOOK WRITES ITS ATTRIBUTE DICE AS "24+2D6" AND THE APP''S GRAMMAR IS
    "2d6+24". The same distribution, written the way `rollAttribute` parses;
    written the book''s way round, `class-check` rejects it as neither dice nor
    a fixed number and says the roller would silently substitute 3d6.
  - An absent ladder on printed 224 is not a verdict: this R.C.C. states that
    player characters use the psi-stalker''s table, which resolves in this
    catalog. Nothing is stored - a Rifts class carries no `xp_table` here.
  - The secondary-skill exclusion (any category except electrical, mechanical,
    medical and science) is not enforced; `secondary_skills` takes a count and
    a schedule and no category restriction. It is in the block''s note.
  - `psionics.type` is deliberately absent, for the reason recorded on the
    Gargoyle: "equal to a 6th level psychic" is a power level rather than a
    minor/major/master tier, and the entry states no psionic save target of its
    own. The +1 to save vs psionic attacks it DOES print is stored.
