# Gurgoyle

## Lore

Gurgoyles are somewhat smaller, wingless versions of gargoyles. They are equally vicious and serve as the foot soldiers of the invading hordes - excellent warriors, ruthless in combat, and familiar with the use of energy weapons. Some of the non-human kingdoms actually manufacture energy weapons for them. It is the gurgoyles who wear plate body armour and who operate the newly developed power armour and giant robots.

Gurgoyles are always submissive and loyal to gargoyle mages, lords and their winged brothers, the gargoyles. Both gurgoyles and gargoyles are carnivores who feast on the flesh of any living creature that falls prey to them, from cattle to humans. Both have a special fondness for vibro-blades, rune weapons and whips or chain weapons. Although gurgoyles and gargoyles possess some psychic abilities, only the gargoyle lords and mages possess great magic or psionic power.

Like the gargoyle, the gurgoyle is a creature from another dimension rather than a true demon, hatched from an egg but warm-blooded, with a pack mentality and a loyalty to its flock that survives even when that flock has been adopted and is composed mostly of non-gargoyles.

## GM Notes

Everything the Gargoyle''s GM notes say about how Europeans treat gargoyles applies to the gurgoyle: most Europeans loathe them regardless of alignment, merchants will not sell to them, and anyone who associates with them is regarded as scum. Asians share the sentiment; the Americas, Canada and Africa care far less, and Atlantis and the New Phoenix Empire welcome them.

Gurgoyles are the ones who actually use the Gargoyle Empire''s technology - the plate armour, the power armour and the giant robots - even though no gurgoyle could build or repair any of it. They know how to use and maintain a device, and they understand its function, value and danger well enough to respond appropriately.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gurgoyle');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gurgoyle';

